From 68c1c8215b8e569e811a2962b3b9d594637031d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:50:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/27] Metal diamond engine: pick the tiling at run time
 (snapshot cg28)

No single tiling is best for every model: in the cg23 and cg27 sweeps the GCPW line and
notch x3 ran best with K=4 tiles 12,8, the SMA launch with K=3 8,6, the patch tutorial
with K=3 6,6, patch x5 and the notch tutorial with the default K=4 8,8, up to 12 % apart.
SetupGPU now builds these four tilings (tile buffers, threads per tile, and a copy of
the extension words followed by the tiling's per-tile lists; the extension floats and
the state stay shared), and IterateTS gives its command buffers the tilings in turn
(half batches, at most two buffers in flight), keeps per tiling the least GPU time per
step of four timed buffers, then runs the fastest and releases the others' buffers.
Timed are full batches and whole IterateTS calls only; the short last buffer of a call
and the first buffer of the run (mapping, warm-up) run the first tiling and do not take
a turn, so the call pattern cannot starve one tiling. Every tiling gives every value
the same operations in the same order (only independent cells change their order), so
the fields do not depend on the choice.

OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TUNE=n: timed buffers per tiling (default 4), 0: K=4 8,8 as before.
OPENEMS_DIAMOND_K, OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TILE and OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TIMING=2 fix one tiling.
Verbose or OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TIMING=1 print the choice and the measured rates.

The tuner picks the best fixed tiling on all six benchmark models, after 532-623 steps.
Against cg27, paired, 5 rounds, quiet Mac (other processes 0.5-1.3 cores): SMA launch
x1.094 (1671 -> 1828 MC/s), GCPW line x1.114 (1896 -> 2113), notch x3 x1.061 (3039 ->
3226), patch tutorial x1.064 (1640 -> 1764), notch tutorial x0.996 and patch x5 x0.995
(the default is best there; the tuning costs under 1 % of these short runs); with
OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TUNE=0 this build is within 0.3 % of cg27 on all six.

emsKit diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 (the 54 before and per box a tuned run that ends its
tuning within the run and one that changes tilings for most of it); all six benchmark
models bit-identical to the multithreaded engine with OPENEMS_FTZ=1.

